# UsageCore

Java 21 + Spring Boot 3 + Maven. PostgreSQL is the transactional source of truth.

## Architecture

- Pragmatic hexagonal/clean architecture.
- Domain must not depend on Spring MVC, Kafka, PostgreSQL, AWS, or HTTP.
- Workloads (long-term): control-plane, entitlement-runtime, usage-pipeline.
- Build only workloads required by the current milestone.
- Kafka only after entitlement-runtime foundation.
- No frontend in this repo. No AI/LLM components.
- Do not add Redis, MongoDB, Elasticsearch, GraphQL, service mesh, or similar without an explicit measured requirement.

## Domain invariants

- Tenant isolation is mandatory.
- At-least-once delivery; never claim end-to-end exactly-once.
- `ContractVersion` activated state is immutable historical commercial evidence.
- Plans are templates; activated contracts never change when plans change.

## Working rules

- Inspect existing code before edits; make bounded changes only.
- Do not rewrite unrelated working code.
- Run relevant validation after every implementation task.
- Fix failures caused by your changes before declaring completion.
- Report commands executed, results, files changed, unresolved risks.
- Never say production-ready without evidence.
- No fabricated test, benchmark, security, or deployment claims.
